.next/
dist/
.DS_Store
# Runtime logs. `*.log.1`/`*.log.2` covered the ROTATIONS but not the live file,
# so `logs/intake-service.log` stayed tracked and carried whole /intake request
# bodies — name, dob, ssn, address, phone — from before DEBT D1 was fixed. The
# content is synthetic (db/seed/*.csv fixtures, not real patients), so this is
# not a breach; it is a PHI-SHAPED artifact in version control, which is the
# habit worth removing rather than the incident worth reporting.
#
# Untracked 2026-08-22. As with `.env` below, history was NOT rewritten: the old
# lines remain in every past commit. The controls are that the data is synthetic
# and that `_intake_log_summary` now logs an allowlist of two keys, so nothing
# new of this shape is written. See tests/fixtures/ for a scrubbed sample to
# quote when an example is needed — never the live file.
*.log
logs/
.venv/
.cache/
.codex_tmp/

# Real environment files carry secrets and must never be committed. `.env` WAS
# tracked until 2026-08-20 and its DB_PASSWORD, PAYER_API_KEY and
# SESSION_SECRET are still recoverable from git history — history was
# deliberately not rewritten, so ROTATION is the control here, not deletion.
# See adr/0007. `.env.example` is the template and stays tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
